WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ We seek refuge in God from Sheytan.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Our teacher today is Mahmoud Sabahi and we'll be working, starting at Sura 74.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Dr. Sabahi (unintelligible)

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Dr. Sabahi: Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem Before starting the Sura, I think, the traditional teachers

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
and students, I'm gonna have a pop quiz next week on what I teach today so that

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:05.000
the ones who sleep and we'll find out about who is listening and who is not. I think maybe

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
tonight is about the anniversary of the time that I came to the mosque last year, or it is

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:19.000
close because I know it from the NBA playoffs. When I came the first night here, there was

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
a gentleman here who had a small TV. He moved to Detroit, I guess, and he had the Lakers,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Dr. Sabahi: and I guess Detroit on TV. So, it's about a year, more or less.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: God has His ways of reminding us of important days.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:44.000
So, and this is a very tough Sura that is given to me, but given the fact that God is the teacher of the Quran,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:54.000
I asked Him to help me tonight, hopefully to be able to do a good job of what I understand from this surah, basically.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.000
And then, I'll give you my views and whatever you think about it,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Then, it can be discussed.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.000
أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.000
One more thing that I have to add. I have, I'm gonna, I have divided the Sura in different parts.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:24.000
I have gone through the whole thing. I've tried to see what the overall point of the

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Sura is, and whether I can divide it in different parts that could help us understand it better.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:42.000
The first 7 verses of the Sura, starting from 1 until 7, it seems to be like

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:52.000
the instructions that God is giving to, a lot of people, I think, to Muhammad, and we know

00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:00.000
that it is not only to Muhammad, it's to everyone, and especially to what we know about the code

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
right now. So, I start with the first verse.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.000
[74:1] O you hidden secret.* [74:2] Come out and warn. [74:3] Extol your Lord. [74:4] Cleanse your cover.*

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
[74:5] Forsake what is wrong. [74:6] Be content with your lot. [74:7] Steadfastly commemorate your Lord.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:24.000
These 7 Ayas, as you see, God is instructing or ordering the secret.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.000
I looked into a lot of translations, Farsi translations. All of them almost unanimously

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:47.000
translate this as "O you, the person who you have covered yourself with some clothing or something",

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.000
which they have taken it literally as someone who is under something covered,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.000
which they think is Muhammad, and this is towards him, telling him that "O you, Muhammad,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:06.000
"you hidden secret, come out and warn, start your mission and bring your message across."

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Especially, this, this may be the third Sura that was revealed to Muhammad. That's what

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:20.000
makes it for a lot of people to believe that this is directly for Muhammad. But now that

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:27.000
we know that Quran is for all times, that doesn't apply to Muhammad. It can apply to

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:40.000
anyone. And it can apply to what we believe is the messenger. Then, God is telling that secret,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
the person, whoever it is, that

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.000
[74:3] Glorify your Lord. [74:4] Cleanse your cover.*

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:54.000
which I had a lot of trouble understanding what does that cleansing mean. It could be a lot of people

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.000
in Farsi translations, they have taken it as cleaning your clothes, because you wanna

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.000
pray, you wanna go to talk to God, so you have to clean your clothes from whatever

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:14.000
is on it, so that it's clean and nice. But basically, it could mean that it is

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:22.000
about the secret that cleanses the message, cleanses the Quran or the religion from whatever it has

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:30.000
been attached to it during these 1400 years. Then, God is asking him to forsake what is

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:39.000
wrong, stay away from the wrong, be content with your lot. This is very crucial. Be happy

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:46.000
with what your God has given you, and always commemorate your Lord. With these 7 Suras, then God is

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:52.000
putting another instruction, that I think is from 8 to 11. God is saying

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:57.000
[74:8] Then, when the horn is blown. [74:9] That will be a difficult day. [74:10] For the disbelievers, not easy.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.000
[74:11] Let Me deal with what I created as an individual.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:11.000
God is here in this Ayas 8 to 11, is telling

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:17.000
the messenger that "when the horn is blown", which is obviously referring to the Day of

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:22.000
Judgment, which is gonna be a difficult day for the disbelievers and a good day

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:29.000
for the believers. He says "that's not gonna be an easy day for those, and let Me deal

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
with those." And this is a very interesting Aya to me at least.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
[74:11] Let Me deal with what I created as an individual.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Sometimes we take it upon ourselves to deal with those who are disbelievers,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:50.000
or who happen not to agree with what we say. And we try to deal with them or make judgments.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:59.000
And I think this is a very good verse that here God is telling us, that "let Me deal with those.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:03.000
"Don't worry about those. I'm gonna deal with them. You worry about what you're supposed to."

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:14.000
Then, from these instructions, the first part, if you look at it, it's all in present

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:21.000
tense. It's like the instructions telling him what to do and what not to do. And then, from

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.000
12 on, it starts with,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.000
[74:12] I provided him with lots of money.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:35.000
I provided these, which is referring I believe to the disbeliever, those individuals that God is saying that I'll deal with them.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:41.000
[74:12] I provided him with lots of money. [74:13] And children to behold. [74:14] I made everything easy for him.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:46.000
[74:15] Yet, he is greedy for more. [74:16] He stubbornly refused to accept these proofs.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:55.000
[74:17] I will increasingly punish him. [74:18] For he reflected, then decided. [74:19] Miserable is what he decided.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.000
[74:20] Miserable indeed is what he decided. [74:21] He looked. [74:22] He frowned and whined.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.000
[74:23] Then he turned away arrogantly. [74:24] He said, "This is but clever magic! [74:25] "This is human made."

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:19.000
I'll stop at 25, because I think between 12 and 25, we have a very interesting description of a disbeliever.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:30.000
God is teaching us and telling us that He has provided those with lots of money,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.000
something that people tend to take as a measure of happiness, as a measure of success.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:48.000
And since God knows that, which is something that human beings are used to, He says that

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.000
[74:12] I provided him with lots of money.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:09:00.000
And then, children. Children are second to money here, as something that

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:10.000
everyone knows that how human beings love to have children. And so, this is another blessing

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:15.000
from God, that in addition to money that God provides for everyone, He provides children.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:16.000
And then He says,

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.000
[74:14] I made everything easy for him.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:27.000
just to test him, I guess, to make sure

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
that everything is provided for him. He says,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.000
[74:14] I made everything easy for him.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:39.000
so that he can reach whatever he likes to. But he's greedy for more. Human beings are greedy.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:49.000
You never are content with what you get, what God provides you, unless you learn to believe in God and

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:58.000
to be happy with what you have. This is something that especially for younger generations, like

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:04.000
my own children, we always have this discussion that, you know, "why don't we have more?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:10.000
"Where is it? Where is it?" So, it never ends. The more you have, the more you want.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:17.000
You can see it everywhere, especially in this country, which is so rich. You see it more and more.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:23.000
People want more and more and more. You read it, you see it on TV, newspapers, every aspect of

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:32.000
of life. It is not only in money, it's in fame, it's in science, it's everywhere.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.000
You know, there are people who are greedy. It doesn't matter what it is. They're greedy for more.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:43.000
They're not happy with what they are. There's a difference between being greedy for more and trying to

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:49.000
reach your potential. So, you shouldn't mix those things up. You have to work hard.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:55.000
God loves the people who work hard, and you can't reach higher grounds. But you always have to

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:00.000
commemorate and remember what God tells you, which we have it at the second part of

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.000
the Sura, at the later part of the Sura.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.000
[74:16] He stubbornly refused to accept these proofs.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.000
God is referring to the proofs that we are gonna go to it later on, that

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.000
he stubbornly refuses to accept those. And we know, we have seen people who do this.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
[74:17] I will increasingly punish him.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.000
Now, God is telling us that what He's gonna do with those disbelievers.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:30.000
"I will punish him", and the reason is that "he reflected, then he decided."

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.000
[74:19] Miserable is what he decided. [74:20] Miserable indeed is ...

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:41.000
he just... God is again stressing of the fact that this decision

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:52.000
of not heeding the warnings and learning and believing in God alone is a miserable decision.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.000
[74:21] He looked. [74:22] He frowned and whined. [74:23] Then he turned away arrogantly.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.000
[74:24] He said, "This is but clever magic! [74:25] "This is human made."

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:04.000
When I was reading these verses and in everyday life

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:12.000
that we go through, I see it's real. It is everyday. It's not something that only

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:18.000
may have happened to Muhammad or God was telling to Muhammad. This is something that happens everyday.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:26.000
Especially since, with my background, coming from a religious family, a Muslim family,

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:32.000
living in Iran, and coming to U.S., getting education, going back during the revolution,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:38.000
and thinking that this is what we wanted, Islamic country. This is what everyone wanted.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:45.000
We were looking, we were striving to have Islam as part of our country, as part of the government.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:52.000
And it has been a tradition. I'm gonna just get away from this for a minute,

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:57.000
which I think is something, I have thought a lot about it, and I think it is

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:03.000
something that would define if I shared with you. We went back home in 1979,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:12.000
which was right after the revolution. I loved to go back because this was something that we loved to see,

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.000
an Islamic government, everything according to what we had the knowledge of Islam, this,

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:27.000
the religion of equality, justice for everyone. And so, everyone was happy, and 96% of the people

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:34.000
voted for Islamic Republic. That was a true vote that happened at that time.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:40.000
And my job was to teach in the university, and the university was the source, the center of all the action,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:47.000
the intellectuals, the educated people. And because of the Islamic

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:51.000
background that all of us have in Iran, in addition to people who were leftist

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:59.000
towards Marxism, there were a lot of groups who had Islamic backgrounds and wanted to have

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:05.000
an Islamic government, but they didn't know what it is. What is... How God wants to run this country,

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:13.000
if it is what He really wants. But every group, there were maybe in a time, I remember, there were

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:21.000
maybe 10 different Islamic groups. Everyone with a different interpretation, not of Quran,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:27.000
of something that they thought is from Quran. Because now I look back and I see that how far

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:33.000
we have been, how far I have been, how far those people have been from the truth. Because

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:39.000
now that I go through this, I still don't know much about Quran, but when I read more,

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:49.000
when I come to studies, I see that this is a different story. And over there, which I think is a good example of

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:55.000
what is happening in all of the Islamic world, is that people take their own

00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:04.000
understanding, which is not complete. They don't have the access to Arabic.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:14.000
They have access to lousy translations. And one interesting thing that I read recently was that somebody

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:25.000
mentioned that people try to interpret Quran or translate Quran based on the Hadith.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:33.000
They mean they adjust the Quran translation or understanding to the Hadith, not vice versa. And this is

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:42.000
a very true thing that happens. But anyway, during these times, always wanting more from

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Islam, wanting to know more from Quran has been something that, especially the younger

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:53.000
generations after Dr. Shariati wanted to know. But unfortunately, there is no way that you

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.000
can reach these things. You can reach the point to see what is really in here.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:07.000
What happened is that people started to think twice after what happened, after two or three years after revolution.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Everybody started to blame Islam and Quran and whatever is related to it.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:20.000
They didn't think that this is because these religious establishments, whose leaders are there,

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:26.000
ruling the country, were representative of Islam. And people who just knew Islam because

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:34.000
they were born as Muslims, they saw this as a true representation of what is really all

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:43.000
about. When you say Islam, you stone a woman. If you see Islam, you execute someone without

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:49.000
any trial. If it's Islam, they can search you without any warrant, anything.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:55.000
They can take you, kill you, and so on and so forth. So, what happened was that after five years, which

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:00.000
I was eligible to come for my sabbatical, four years after I came to U.S. for a

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.000
presentation of a paper to a conference. Then as a matter of fact, I came to Tucson to visit a friend.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.000
Then, I went back home and I told Mary that I have to go for sabbatical leave.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:15.000
I'm sick and tired of... I want to learn more science, so I have to go. So, I started

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:20.000
to look for... Sabbatical leave is something that everybody who works in university

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:27.000
after so many years is eligible to go for extension of their education or

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:34.000
catching up with the science to update their knowledge. After revolution, they have completely

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:39.000
demolished it. But when I went back home, I said, Mary, we have to go. Whatever happens,

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:48.000
we want to go, we should go. And God knows now that I know after a few months, they passed the rule that now people can go.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:55.000
And since I was one of the older, at least at the time, had more experience at the university,

00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:01.000
I applied and was accepted. And it was a big, long journey to come to U.S. And we almost stopped

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:07.000
in Vancouver, but things worked out, and thanks God we ended up in Tucson. But when we came here,

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:13.000
one thing that I didn't wanna hear about was Islam, Quran, and everything.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:21.000
The reason was that I saw the brainwashings that were going on in schools. I leave my children in school, and

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:27.000
it was a dilemma. What could I teach them? What is being taught in the schools?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:31.000
And what contradictions and what problems and what dangers are involved?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:38.000
So, anyway, we came here, and I remember one day one of these Jehovah's Witnesses came to the door

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:44.000
and talked to her. She couldn't refuse. She's so nice, she talked to them. And after

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.000
they kept calling, she said "Mahmoud, talk to them, tell them 'you don't wanna hear it.'"

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:56.000
And I said "you invited them, why should I?" One Sunday morning, they showed up at the door, two very nice ladies.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:01.000
I opened the door, I had the chain on, I said "no, we don't wanna talk to you."

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:05.000
The lady insisted. I felt bad. I said "okay, let's make an arrangement for another week."

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:11.000
So anyway, one day they came in. I sat down with them, I said "okay, I listen to you. Give all of your things."

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:17.000
She started, you know, giving all the ceremonies, whatever

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:21.000
she wanted to talk about. And I said "see, I'm coming from a religious country.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:31.000
"I've lived five years under Khomeini. I have decided that I'm gonna be away from any religion for the rest of my life.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:37.000
"What you're saying is exactly what Khomeini said, and they're similar. I don't wanna hear it, please don't bother us."

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.000
The lady was shocked, so they left. They never came back.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:50.000
It took about three years, I guess, that all of a sudden we realized that something is missing.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:59.000
The missing part was that I saw my children growing, and I had the privilege to be raised in a religious family.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:06.000
To learn this, either from school, either my parents see them, and practice religion. But you know,...

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:19.000
And we looked around and I said "God, something wrong is happening." And I knew that there was no way that I could go anywhere else.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:25.000
And I didn't know about this mosque at all. Somehow Mary found out about it, and she said, she came sooner than me, as a matter of fact.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:38.000
And then one night, she said "okay, let's go, you know, try it, you know, it's not gonna hurt." And I came, I came a few nights, and I listened.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:47.000
One thing that impressed me the most was the fact that the message was strong.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:56.000
"Worship God alone. Forget about everything else." And one night, I remember, I asked, because I had heard from

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:03.000
other friends that, you know, this is... The person, which was Dr. Khalifa, is saying he's a messenger of God.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:10.000
How can it be? We have the Khatam Al-Nabiyyin (خَاتَمَ ٱلنَّبِيِّـۧنَ), it is impossible that somebody else could be.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:15.000
And I asked him, I remember, in one of these studies, I said "why you say you are the messenger of God?"

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:22.000
And I don't know whether he remembers what he answered me or not, but his answer was great for me, and he said

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:27.000
"Messenger doesn't mean" something in this, I'm not quote-unquote exactly saying what you said.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:36.000
But he said "Messenger is not important. What is important is the message. If you like the message, take it, if you don't like it, so leave it."

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Which the message was something that I liked, and I have been here since then.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:49.000
So, nowadays, my friends here, a lot of them are very puzzled, I see.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:58.000
One of them, who I was talking recently to, he doesn't practice either. You know, he says he doesn't believe in anything.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.000
But one thing, very interestingly that he asked me, he said,

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:07.000
"Why among all those mosques, you go to this mosque?" And I said

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:13.000
"What does it have to do with you? Because you say you don't believe in God." He didn't say he doesn't believe in God. I pushed him

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:16.000
and I said "okay. You say you don't believe in God." He said "no, no, I believe in God."

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:21.000
He was scared to say that. But he said "Muhammad wrote Quran.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:28.000
"He just wrote it himself. He did everything, and these are all a bunch of", his word, "nonsense."

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:33.000
