01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:32.000
A man: You wanted questions. Dr. Sabahi: Comments. Give comments.

01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:39.000
A man: About making judgment about others.

01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:47.000
A man: I think the function of the person who's making judgment, all the time, every second, you're making judgement

01:02:47.000 --> 01:02:55.000
about things, about people, about everything. So, if you mean that, if you make a judgement

01:02:55.000 --> 01:02:58.000
without having any proof, do not disclose it to others.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:09.000
But in your day-to-day life, you love one person more than the other. This is just based on your personal judgment.

01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:16.000
You feel one person is more reverent than the other. You get more close to him than the other.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:24.000
This is just based on your personal judgment. But I agree that if you don't have enough...

01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:29.000
If you don't have enough evidence, you should not disclose it to somebody else that "this guy is not Mu'min (believer)."

01:03:29.000 --> 01:03:34.000
Because this is illegal, if you don't have enough evidence. Or, you cannot prosecute.

01:03:34.000 --> 01:03:42.000
That's, that is the function of God. God will prosecute or make judgment, final judgment on any,

01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:48.000
A man: whoever He wills. If that's you mean by different....But personal judgment, you are doing every second.

01:03:50.000 --> 01:03:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, this is a very important point, because they make a big deal here about "don't judge."

01:03:56.000 --> 01:04:01.000
Well, you cannot say the person is going to Heaven or Hell. This is what you cannot do.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:07.000
Because people change. You can change tomorrow. Remember Dr. Sabahi himself made a statement that somebody

01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:11.000
doesn't believe in God. It's a statement of fact. The person himself said "I don't believe in God."

01:04:12.000 --> 01:04:15.000
But we don't know if this person is going to Hell or Heaven, because tomorrow, he may believe better than me.

01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:20.000
And so, this is where you cannot judge in that respect, but you can,

01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:28.000
like you said, you make judgments all day, based on the Quran and certain criteria.

01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:33.000
If the person himself says "I don't believe in God", you can say "this person does not believe in God."

01:04:34.000 --> 01:04:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: And this is not judgment.

01:04:36.000 --> 01:04:38.000
Edip: (unintelligible)

01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: You can say "if he continues like this and dies as disbeliever in God, he will go to Hell." That's what God said.

01:04:44.000 --> 01:04:53.000
But you cannot say "this person is going to Hell or Heaven without any basis. Because this is a changing possibility.

01:04:53.000 --> 01:04:57.000
A man: They even cannot disclose it. I think it's not good to disclose to somebody else.

01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:10.000
A man: People oftentimes, though, when you're talking about, like, personal judgments even, there's, you find a lot of fault in them,

01:05:10.000 --> 01:05:15.000
because oftentimes, you draw conclusions. Somebody says something, well, I don't do this, and then

01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:22.000
A man: you know, you make assumptions which is... So, judging all the way around. That's all you have to worry about it yourself. Dr. Khalifa: That's (unintelligible).

01:05:22.000 --> 01:05:24.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible) assumptions that's are just... A man: Oh, just... yeah, well like if you...

01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:36.000
A man: It's a natural tendency that if you see this and you see this, well people

01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:42.000
make conclusions, or they assume that, you know, one and two, well, that makes three. But you don't know for sure,

01:05:42.000 --> 01:05:49.000
you know just because it's a human tendency to draw conclusions from, you know, other examples or

01:05:49.000 --> 01:05:54.000
things that may have affected you in your life, but it may not be true for all circumstances.

01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly. This is a very important principle in the Quran that we must always remember,

01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:03.000
that a little bit of suspicion is sinful. Even a little bit is sinful.

01:06:04.000 --> 01:06:10.000
If a person is passing by you and making a face, you draw a conclusion that this person is unfriendly or doesn't like you.

01:06:11.000 --> 01:06:17.000
Based on that, you can be wrong, and it is sinful, because that person could be having a headache or a stomachache.

01:06:17.000 --> 01:06:19.000
You don't know why he's making a face.

01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:26.000
And you must give the person the benefit of doubt. Instead of stating that the person is unfriendly or doesn't like you,

01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:29.000
you have to say that something is bothering this person.

01:06:29.000 --> 01:06:35.000
And you feel more, actually, pity or kindness towards the person instead of the other way around.

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:43.000
So, the Quran makes this very clear, very strong. A little bit of suspicion is sinful.

01:06:43.000 --> 01:06:47.000
You cannot make conclusions or assumptions without proof.

01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:50.000
A man: Can I make a comment here?

01:06:51.000 --> 01:06:59.000
A man: Like, some people think that if a person doesn't come to the mosque and pray, he prays in the afternoons and people come at 12, and some of them cannot come.

01:06:59.000 --> 01:07:04.000
And people think that only because we don't come, you know, we don't pray

01:07:04.000 --> 01:07:10.000
you know, because we always have to be here or something. You know, it doesn't have to be that we don't pray.

01:07:10.000 --> 01:07:15.000
We can pray when we're working or something like that. So, it doesn't mean that we don't pray.

01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:22.000
A man: Or that we don't have to do something. Like I missed a lot of (unintelligible).

01:07:22.000 --> 01:07:24.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible) A man: Yeah.

01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's, that's a sin.

01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: You shouldn't miss Quranic studies or prayers.

01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:31.000
A man: No. Well, I was working. Sure.

01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, okay. You have an excuse.

01:07:35.000 --> 01:07:40.000
A man: It doesn't mean that you're not trying to do your best to come or do something, you know.

01:07:40.000 --> 01:07:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: They're excuses. That's it.

01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible) Dr. Sabahi.

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:48.000
Dr. Sabahi: I think I want us to continue. No, I'm not gonna answer,

01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:52.000
because I wanna go and finish as much as I can. Then at the end, I will do it, because I think

01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:59.000
it's very important to get to the later part of the Sura, which is kind of interesting

01:07:59.000 --> 01:08:09.000
the way it is worded. 32 to 39. Again, it's in the present tense.

01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:18.000
[74:32] Absolutely, (I swear) by the moon. [74:33] And the night as it passes. [74:34] And the morning as it shines.

01:08:19.000 --> 01:08:21.000
[74:35] This is one of the great miracles.*

01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:26.000
[74:36] A warning to the human race. [74:37] For those among you who wish to advance, or regress.

01:08:26.000 --> 01:08:31.000
[74:38] Every soul is trapped by its sins. [74:39] Except for those on the right.

01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:42.000
Again, if you put this, if you not try to isolate verses from each other, you see clearly that

01:08:42.000 --> 01:08:50.000
God in 32, 33 and 34 is swearing even to human beings that

01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:55.000
[74:32] ... (I swear) by the moon. [74:33] By the night as it passes.

01:08:55.000 --> 01:09:00.000
because these are the things that we see, we feel, we experience everyday.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:05.000
[74:34] And the morning as it shines. [74:35] This is one of the great miracles.*

01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:14.000
This is referring exactly to 31 that God is talking about 19 angels and the number 19.

01:09:14.000 --> 01:09:19.000
And God is swearing that this is one of the greatest miracles. And

01:09:23.000 --> 01:09:34.000
verse 36 is telling us that this is a warning to human race which could apply to any way, at any period of time as we know it.

01:09:34.000 --> 01:09:37.000
And, and

01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:40.000
[74:37] For those among you who wish to advance, or regress.

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:50.000
We have the choice. If we see the miracle, if we follow the Quran, then we advance. Otherwise, we regress. And it says,

01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:52.000
[74:38] Every soul is trapped by its sins.

01:09:52.000 --> 01:09:56.000
The more you commit sins, the more you are gonna be trapped.

01:09:56.000 --> 01:10:00.000
The more you will have a difficult time to get out of it. And this goes back to

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:09.000
what has been discussed quite a few number of times here that 40 years of age is the limit.

01:10:09.000 --> 01:10:14.000
But are we free to do everything up to that point? But I guess here

01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:15.000
[74:38] Every soul is trapped by its sins.

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:20.000
The more you sin, the more you get trapped into it. The harder it is to get out.

01:10:20.000 --> 01:10:26.000
And so, it is something that the progress has to be made by time.

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:40.000
Then, from 39 to I guess to 47, God is explaining what will happen in the future.

01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:44.000
[74:39] Except for those on the right. [74:40] While in Paradise, ...

01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:45.000
The ones was on the right.

01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:50.000
[74:40] While in Paradise, they will ask. [74:41] About the guilty.

01:10:50.000 --> 01:10:56.000
[74:42] "What brought you to this retribution?" [74:43] They will say, "We did not observe the contact prayers (Salat).

01:10:56.000 --> 01:11:02.000
[74:44] "We did not feed the poor. [74:45] "We blundered with the blunderers. [74:46] "We disbelieved in the Day of Judgment.

01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:04.000
[74:47] "Until certainty came to us now."

01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:12.000
If we compare these verses 40 to 47,

01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:20.000
God is giving the reasons for people who go to the Hell. Basically, these are the things that

01:11:20.000 --> 01:11:26.000
have been said over and over here in the studies or in the Khutbahs that

01:11:26.000 --> 01:11:28.000
God is giving the reasons to say,

01:11:28.000 --> 01:11:33.000
[74:43] They will say, "We did not observe the contact prayers (Salat). [74:44] "We did not feed the poor.

01:11:33.000 --> 01:11:34.000
The Zakat.

01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:38.000
[74:45] "We blundered with the blunderers. [74:46] "We disbelieved in the Day of Judgment.

01:11:38.000 --> 01:11:42.000
So, these are the major that you can commit.

01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:48.000
And then, you deserve Hell. And then, when in the Day of Judgment,

01:11:48.000 --> 01:11:56.000
when you are in there, certainty came to you, it's too late. You have already committed enough

01:11:56.000 --> 01:12:08.000
that it's too late for you to repent. And God now is saying, it's a kind of closing on the whole Sura. God is saying,

01:12:08.000 --> 01:12:11.000
[74:48] The intercession of the intercessors will never help them.

01:12:11.000 --> 01:12:14.000
Because of what they committed, the sins that they committed.

01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:20.000
[74:49] Why are they so averse to this reminder? [74:50] Running like zebras. [74:51] Who are fleeing from the lion!

01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:30.000
[74:52] Does each one of them want to receive the scripture personally? [74:53] Indeed, they do not fear the Hereafter. [74:54] Indeed, this is a reminder.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:40.000
[74:55] For those who wish to take heed. [74:56] They cannot take heed against GOD's will. He is the source of righteousness; He is the source of forgiveness.

01:12:41.000 --> 01:12:51.000
48 is clearly what I didn't know before coming to the mosque that Shafa'at or intercession is not gonna help anyone.

01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:57.000
That's why a lot of people who think they are Muslims, they believe in

01:12:57.000 --> 01:13:03.000
intercession by Muhammad, by his followers, Ali and maybe Omar and so on and so forth.

01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:09.000
But clearly, God is saying that no Shafa'at, no intercession. And then, God is kind of,

01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:18.000
when I read this verse, it's kind of a son, a father talking to his son, because I have a son, 2 sons. It say

01:13:18.000 --> 01:13:20.000
[74:49] Why are they so averse to this reminder?

01:13:20.000 --> 01:13:26.000
Because you tell your son, because you are more experienced, you have a little more gray hair. And you say "don't do this."

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:32.000
God is telling us "don't do this. Do the right things." But we are averse to the reminder.

01:13:32.000 --> 01:13:36.000
And then, we go and experience it. And God says, you know,

01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:39.000
[74:49] Why are they so averse to this reminder?

01:13:39.000 --> 01:13:46.000
Why they don't take heed and they don't understand? They are running like zebras who are fleeing from lion.

01:13:48.000 --> 01:13:55.000
And then, God is asking, I think there's a little bit sarcasm in here, that

01:13:55.000 --> 01:13:58.000
[74:52] Does each one of them want to receive the scripture personally?

01:13:58.000 --> 01:14:03.000
Should God come to each one of us personally and tell "okay, this is your Scripture. Go and follow these rules."

01:14:03.000 --> 01:14:07.000
And then, God is telling us,

01:14:07.000 --> 01:14:09.000
[74:53] Indeed, they do not fear the Hereafter.

01:14:10.000 --> 01:14:17.000
They are not afraid of the Day of Judgment. Indeed, this is a reminder. This book, this message,

01:14:17.000 --> 01:14:23.000
Dr. Sabahi: this miracle is a reminder for all the people. For those...

01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:24.000
Dr. Sabahi: Oh,...

01:14:24.000 --> 01:14:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: You're alright?

01:14:29.000 --> 01:14:30.000
A woman: Are you Ok?

01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:33.000
A man: I think it came down on him.

01:14:34.000 --> 01:14:35.000
Dr. Sabahi: Are you Ok?

01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: See God protects you.

01:14:55.000 --> 01:14:57.000
Dr. Sabahi: You should have come down directly.

01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:10.000
[74:54] Indeed, this is a reminder. [74:55] For those who wish to take heed. [74:56] They cannot take heed against GOD's will. He is the source of righteousness; He is the source of forgiveness.

01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:17.000
These have been discussed before here. And since there's only five minutes, I'm gonna stop.

01:15:17.000 --> 01:15:21.000
There are a few verses that I took out of other places that would support what is here,

01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:30.000
which I'm gonna quote here and then leave for questions and answers.

01:15:32.000 --> 01:15:34.000
Dr. Sabahi: Edip, you can ask your question.

01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:38.000
Edip: I forgot my question.

01:15:38.000 --> 01:15:40.000
Dr. Sabahi: That was the whole purpose.

01:15:41.000 --> 01:15:45.000
Edip: Your question is up. My question is

01:15:46.000 --> 01:15:53.000
Edip: When hypocrites appear, when they feel advantage in any community, they appear.

01:15:54.000 --> 01:16:03.000
And during the first beginning of revelation, there was no any hypocrite.

01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:09.000
There shouldn't be, because there is no benefit to become Muslim. Many Muslims are under torture.

01:16:09.000 --> 01:16:19.000
Some of them hide their (unintelligible) persecution. But here, this is a hint that this is a prophecy of Quran.

01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:24.000
(unintelligible) describes (unintelligible). It says,

01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:28.000
(74:31) وَلِيَقُولَ ٱلَّذِينَ فِى قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌۭ وَٱلْكَـٰفِرُونَ مَاذَآ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ

01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:34.000
So, to expose those who harbor doubts in their hearts.

01:16:34.000 --> 01:16:36.000
فِى قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌۭ

01:16:36.000 --> 01:16:44.000
The people who have disease in their hearts. This description is used in the whole Quran for the description

01:16:44.000 --> 01:16:49.000
to describe hypocrite. But during this time of revelation, the revelation of this chapter,

01:16:49.000 --> 01:16:53.000
Edip: there was no hypocrite. This is, this shows that this is

01:16:55.000 --> 01:16:56.000
Dr. Sabahi: For the future.

01:16:56.000 --> 01:16:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible) of Quran. Edip: Yes.

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:05.000
Edip: Another interesting point is, they say,

01:17:05.000 --> 01:17:07.000
[74:46] "We disbelieved in the Day of Judgment.

01:17:07.000 --> 01:17:11.000
But, two verse after this, Allah says,

01:17:11.000 --> 01:17:15.000
[74:48] The intercession of the intercessors will never help them.

01:17:15.000 --> 01:17:24.000
If you believe in intercession, it shows that you believe in Resurrection also. Because you believe in the intercession,

01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:30.000
you say when you resurrect, somebody will save you from God. Is there any contradiction

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:38.000
in these verses? No. You see, they disbelieve in the Day of Judgment. What is the Day of Judgment?

01:17:39.000 --> 01:17:44.000
The description of Day of Judgment, we see in Quran, we see, there is no Shafa'at

01:17:44.000 --> 01:17:52.000
in that day. If you believe in Shafa'at, intercession, you deny, you disbelieve, you are disbeliever of Day of Judgment.

01:17:52.000 --> 01:17:53.000
Because Allah says,

01:17:53.000 --> 01:18:00.000
(82:18) ثُمَّ مَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ (82:19) يَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌۭ لِّنَفْسٍۢ شَيْـًۭٔا ۖ وَٱلْأَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ لِّلَّهِ

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:05.000
On that day, nobody has any power, has no any power.

01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:15.000
All power is power of God. And, if somebody believe in Shafa'at, yes, he doesn't believe in Day of Judgment.

01:18:16.000 --> 01:18:21.000
Edip: If he says, he is only (unintelligible). Dr. Sabahi: Mã Shã Allãh

01:18:22.000 --> 01:18:35.000
Edip: Because, I think, both Muslims, so-called Muslim, and also rejecter of, or atheist, both of them are addressed in these verses.

01:18:36.000 --> 01:18:41.000
Some people may understand, Allah excuse so-called Muslim because

01:18:41.000 --> 01:18:46.000
they say "we believe in Day of Judgment." But in fact, they do not believe in Day of Judgment.

01:18:54.000 --> 01:19:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Do you understand Edip's point about the hypocrites? The hypocrites show up only later, when, when the new message

01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:15.000
from God is strong and generally accepted. But in the initial times, of the elite of the elite, the first believers,

01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:22.000
when there's persecution of the believers, why will the hypocrites be attracted to a place where they are being persecuted, and threatened

01:19:22.000 --> 01:19:26.000
and things like that. So, there's no hypocrites at that time. Because if you announce

01:19:26.000 --> 01:19:33.000
that everyone who comes to Masjid Tucson, we'll give him $200, you know, we have big crowds here,

01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:36.000
and you can be sure some of them are hypocrites. You know they are not all believers.

01:19:37.000 --> 01:19:41.000
When there is persecution and difficult times, there are no hypocrites.

01:19:41.000 --> 01:19:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Okay, we thank you very much, Dr. Sabahi. It was very enlightening. Well, I have to ask you to give us the Khutba next Friday, IN SHAA ALLAH.

01:19:48.000 --> 01:19:49.000
Dr. Sabahi: No, no, please. Dr. Khalifa: You are fantastic.

01:19:52.000 --> 01:19:56.000
Audience: Do it. Do it. Do it.

